<p class="sg-note">Storage source: <?=htmlspecialchars($status['source'])?> — <?=$status['encrypted_hint']?'<span class="sg-ok">encryption hint detected</span>':'<span class="sg-warn">encryption not confirmed</span>'?>.</p>
</div>
<div class="sg-card <?=$settings['STORAGE_MODE']==='vault'?'':'sg-danger'?>">
<h3>Encrypted Vault</h3>
<div class="sg-grid"><div>Initialized: <?=$crypto['initialized']?'<span class="sg-ok">yes</span>':'no'?><br>Unlocked this boot: <?=$crypto['unlocked']?'<span class="sg-ok">yes</span>':'<span class="sg-warn">no</span>'?><br>Preferred crypto: <?=$crypto['sodium']?'Argon2id + authenticated sodium encryption':($crypto['openssl']?'PBKDF2 + AES-256-GCM':'<span class="sg-error">no supported crypto backend</span>')?></div>
<div><strong>Important:</strong> Vault mode protects SecretGuard's files at rest. If Docker's own storage is unencrypted, environment values can still be persisted in Docker container metadata after a container is created. For the strongest protection, use encrypted Docker storage or application-supported file secrets.</div></div>
<?php if(!$crypto['initialized']):?>
<form method="post" style="margin-top:12px"><input type="hidden" name="csrf_token" value="<?=htmlspecialchars($var['csrf_token'])?>"><input type="hidden" name="action" value="init_vault"><input type="password" name="master_password" placeholder="New master password" autocomplete="new-password" required> <input type="password" name="master_password_confirm" placeholder="Confirm master password" autocomplete="new-password" required> <button type="submit">Initialize vault</button></form>
<?php else:?>
<?php if(!$crypto['unlocked']):?><form method="post" style="margin-top:12px"><input type="hidden" name="csrf_token" value="<?=htmlspecialchars($var['csrf_token'])?>"><input type="hidden" name="action" value="unlock_vault"><input type="password" name="master_password" placeholder="Vault master password" autocomplete="current-password" required> <button type="submit">Unlock & restore runtime envs</button></form><?php else:?><form method="post" style="margin-top:12px"><input type="hidden" name="csrf_token" value="<?=htmlspecialchars($var['csrf_token'])?>"><input type="hidden" name="action" value="lock_vault"><button type="submit">Lock vault now</button></form><?php endif;?>
<?php endif;?><p class="sg-note">The password is never written to flash. While unlocked, only a derived 256-bit key is kept at <code>/run/unraid-secretguard/master.key</code>; <code>/run</code> is volatile and disappears on reboot.</p></div>
<div class="sg-card"><h3>Protection overview</h3><p class="sg-note">Installed containers and their SecretGuard status. <strong>Protected</strong> means the active Unraid template points at a SecretGuard-managed env source.</p>
<table class="sg-table sg-overview"><thead><tr><th>Container</th><th>Status</th><th>Mode</th><th>Protected variables</th><th>Action</th></tr></thead><tbody>
<?php foreach($overview as $o):?><tr><td><strong><?=htmlspecialchars($o['container'])?></strong></td><td><?=$o['protected']?'<span class="sg-badge sg-badge-ok">Protected</span>':'<span class="sg-badge sg-badge-off">Not protected</span>'?></td><td><?=$o['protected']?htmlspecialchars($o['mode']):'—'?></td><td><?php if(!$o['protected']):?>—<?php elseif($o['secret_count']===null):?>hidden / unavailable<?php else:?><strong><?=intval($o['secret_count'])?></strong><?php if(!empty($o['secret_names'])):?><br><span class="sg-note"><code><?=htmlspecialchars(implode(', ',$o['secret_names']))?></code></span><?php endif;?><?php endif;?></td><td><?php if($o['protected']&&$o['rollback_available']):?><form method="post" class="sg-inline"><input type="hidden" name="csrf_token" value="<?=htmlspecialchars($var['csrf_token'])?>"><input type="hidden" name="action" value="rollback"><input type="hidden" name="template" value="<?=htmlspecialchars(base64_encode($o['file']))?>"><button type="submit" onclick="return confirm('Rollback SecretGuard for <?=htmlspecialchars(addslashes($o['container']))?>? Only the variables stored in the SecretGuard env file will be restored to the XML template. The env/vault file will then be removed and the container recreated. Other template changes are left untouched.');">Rollback</button></form><?php elseif($o['protected']&&$o['legacy']):?><span class="sg-warn">Legacy env: no variable metadata</span><?php elseif($o['protected']):?><span class="sg-warn">Rollback unavailable</span><?php else:?>—<?php endif;?></td></tr><?php endforeach;?>
</tbody></table><p class="sg-note">Rollback is variable-level: SecretGuard restores only the protected variables from metadata stored alongside them in the env/vault file. It does not restore an old XML snapshot and does not overwrite unrelated ports, paths, labels, or settings.</p></div>
<div class="sg-card"><h3>Docker template audit</h3><p class="sg-note"><strong>Installed containers only:</strong> SecretGuard ignores stale/unused XML templates that do not match a container returned by <code>docker ps -a</code>.</p><p class="sg-note">SecretGuard never displays secret values. High-confidence values are preselected, but migration always requires your confirmation. Each migrated variable stores its original Docker-template attributes and description as comments in the managed env data, enabling a precise rollback without XML backups.</p></div>
<?php foreach($groups as $container=>$items):?>
<div class="sg-card"><div class="sg-container"><?=htmlspecialchars($container)?></div><form method="post"><input type="hidden" name="csrf_token" value="<?=htmlspecialchars($var['csrf_token'])?>"><input type="hidden" name="action" value="migrate"><input type="hidden" name="template" value="<?=htmlspecialchars(base64_encode($items[0]['file']))?>"><table class="sg-table sg-audit-table"><thead><tr><th>Move</th><th>Variable</th><th>Risk</th><th>Value</th><th>Reason</th></tr></thead><tbody>
<?php foreach($items as $r):?><tr><td><?php if($r['classification']==='high'||$r['classification']==='medium'):?><input type="checkbox" name="targets[]" value="<?=htmlspecialchars($r['target'])?>" <?=$r['classification']==='high'&&$r['has_value']?'checked':''?>><?php endif;?></td><td><code><?=htmlspecialchars($r['target'])?></code></td><td class="sg-<?=htmlspecialchars($r['classification'])?>"><?=htmlspecialchars(strtoupper($r['classification']))?></td><td><?=$r['has_value']?'set (hidden)':'empty'?></td><td><?=htmlspecialchars($r['reason'])?></td></tr><?php endforeach;?>
</tbody></table><div class="sg-actions"><button type="submit" onclick="return confirm('Protect selected variables and remove them from this Docker XML template?');">Protect selected secrets & recreate container</button></div></form></div>
<?php endforeach;?>
